 "intro_text": "A frontispiece in books is a decorative or informative illustration facing a book's title page, usually on the left-hand, or verso, page opposite the right-hand, or recto page of a book. \nIn some ancient editions or in modern luxury editions, the frontispiece features thematic or allegorical elements; in others, the author's portrait appears as the frontispiece. \nIn medieval illuminated manuscripts, a presentation miniature showing the book or text being presented (by whom and to whom varies) was often used as a frontispiece.",
 "key": "en/Book_frontispiece",
